+<p align=center><font face="Arial">IN THE ORIGINAL JURISDICTION</font></p>
+<hr width="20%" noshade>
+<p align="center"><font face="Arial">Opinion No. 25508<br>
+Reheard April 2, 2003 - Refiled August 18, 2003</font></p>
+<hr width="20%" noshade>
+<blockquote>
+  <blockquote>
+    <blockquote>
+      <blockquote>
+<p align="left"><font face="Arial">David A. Wilson, of Horton, Drawdy, Ward &amp; Jenkins, of Greenville, for 
+  petitioner.</font></p>
+<p align="left"><font face="Arial">Attorney General Henry D. McMaster, Deputy Attorney General Treva G. Ashworth, 
+  and Assistant Deputy Attorney General J. Emory Smith, Jr., all of Columbia, 
+  for respondent.</font></p>
+<p align="left"><font face="Arial">John T. Moore, C. Mitchell Brown and B. Rush Smith, III, all of Nelson, Mullins, 
+  Riley &amp; Scarborough, of Columbia, for Intervenor South Carolina Bankers 
+  Association.</font></p>
+<p align="left"><font face="Arial">John S. Nichols, of Bluestein &amp; Nichols, of Columbia; and F. Earl Ellis, 
+  Jr., of Ellis, Lawhorne &amp; Sims, of Columbia, for Intervenor South Carolina 
+  Bar.</font></p>
+<p align="left"><font face="Arial">Edward G. Menzie and Brian C. Bonner, both of Nexsen, Pruet, Jacobs &amp; Pollard, 
+  of Columbia, for Amicus Curiae American Financial Services Associates.</font></p>
