+	(A) A person making rent or royalty payments to a nonresident of twelve hundred dollars in any calendar year or more annually for the use or privilege of using property in this State shall withhold a percentage equal to the maximum individual tax rate of each payment to a nonresident individual, partnership, trust, or estate and five percent of each payment to a nonresident corporation or any other nonresident entity.<br /><br />
+	(B) This section does not apply:<br /><br />
+	(1) to a person for the rental of residential housing units, including short-term rentals, when four or fewer units are owned by the nonresident;<br /><br />
